---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Support — Life2Film"
  description="Get help with Life2Film, report a bug, or ask a question."
  basePath="/support"
>
  <main>
    <section>
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h1>Support</h1>
        <p>Something broken, confusing, or missing? Write to us — a real person reads it.</p>

        <p class="mail"><a href="mailto:info@superduperai.co">info@superduperai.co</a></p>

        <p class="muted">
          When reporting a problem, include your device model, iOS version, and what you were doing
          when it happened. If a montage came out wrong, say roughly how many clips were involved
          and what you asked for.
        </p>

        <h2>Common questions</h2>

        <h3>Do I need an account?</h3>
        <p>No. The app works without signing in.</p>

        <h3>Do my videos get uploaded?</h3>
        <p>
          No. Analysis and editing run on your device; originals never leave it. Details in the
          <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>Do I need an API key?</h3>
        <p>
          Only for the AI director. Without one the app still builds montages with its deterministic
          pipeline. With one, requests go straight from your device to the provider you chose.
        </p>

        <h3>Why does the app ask for photo access?</h3>
        <p>It edits videos already in your library. Without access there is nothing to work with.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 44px); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  h3 { margin: 22px 0 6px; font-size: 17px; }
  .mail { font-size: 20px; margin: 22px 0; }
  .mail a { color: var(--cyan); text-decoration: none; }
</style>
